  "notes": "{崩|くず}れる is an intransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}) meaning to fall apart or lose form.\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR: {崩|くず}す (to break down, demolish)\n- {崩|くず}れる: The tower collapses.\n- {崩|くず}す: I knock over the tower.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{崩|くず}れている indicates something has collapsed and remains in that state.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [structure]が{崩|くず}れる — [structure] collapses\n- [plan/health]が{崩|くず}れる — [plan/health] falls apart\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {山|やま}が{崩|くず}れる (mountain collapses - landslide)\n- {天気|てんき}が{崩|くず}れる (weather deteriorates)\n- {体調|たいちょう}を{崩|くず}す (to get sick - transitive form)\n- {姿勢|しせい}が{崩|くず}れる (posture breaks down)\n\nNOTE: The expression {体調|たいちょう}を{崩|くず}す uses the transitive form to mean \"to become ill.\"",
